# Allowlist: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` from the local working tree (not from git), so anything
# dropped into the tree by mistake (case data, evidence, .env, databases) would otherwise be baked
# into the image. Start from nothing and add back only what the image runs.
*

!app/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini
!scripts/
!data/fixtures/demo_case.json
!data/catalogue/channels.json
!requirements.txt
!pyproject.toml
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Hard rules inside the allowed directories (last match wins, so these come after the re-includes).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/case-data
**/*-private
**/deliverables
**/evidence
**/vault
**/exports
**/denylist*.txt
**/masking-map*.json
**/*.docx
**/*.doc
**/*.pdf
**/*.eml
**/*.msg
**/*.heic
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.png
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.zip
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
